REJECT

- **P1 — Published contents are invalidated:** `rust/crates/vexel-platform-apple/src/native_window/window.rs:113,122` calls `setNeedsDisplay()` after installing or restoring the image. Apple documents that this recaches the layer and removes existing contents. `NativeView` provides no drawing/update implementation that reinstalls the frame. Use a presenter-owned layer or an explicit view update path, and remove this invalidation from direct contents publication. [Apple documentation](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/quartzcore/calayer/setneedsdisplay%28%29?changes=_11&language=objc)

- **P1 — Rollback does not guarantee atomic failure:** `rust/crates/vexel-platform-apple/src/native_window/window.rs:101–123` mutates three properties sequentially, then discards every restoration error. A publication failure followed by a restoration failure can leave replacement contents or mixed state installed. Make failure preservation enforceable and add focused fault-injection coverage for each mutation and rollback failure. Correct the unconditional restoration claims at `rust/crates/vexel-platform-apple/README.md:18–20` and `artifacts/WO-RUST-APPLE-PRESENTATION-01/verification.json:31`.

- **P2 — Test evidence is aggregate-only:** `artifacts/WO-RUST-APPLE-PRESENTATION-01/test.log:4–8` contains summarized totals rather than exact Cargo test output. Preserve the original command output, including test names, individual outcomes and exit status, so the claimed 47 passing cases are independently auditable.

- **P2 — Specify the missing runtime proof:** `artifacts/WO-RUST-APPLE-PRESENTATION-01/verification.json:33` records only a general live-rendering limitation. Explicitly record that displayed channel order, top-left orientation, sRGB/alpha compositing, image retention after return, replacement/release behavior, resize/backing-scale replacement, teardown and native exception/rollback behavior remain unverified. The six frame tests at `rust/crates/vexel-platform-apple/src/native_window/frame.rs:96–140` exercise validation and one arithmetic conversion; they do not establish these runtime properties.
